Ze-Reviewed-Against: github.com/opencontainers/runc v1.5.3

H-5 of the runc series: the checkpoint and restore client (criu_linux.go)
compiles only under the build tag runc_criu, and the file that refuses both
calls (criu_disabled_linux.go) compiles without it. Upstream has it the other
way round: the client is built unless the tag runc_nocriu is set.

Ze derives its build tags from feature-gates.txt, and only tags with the ze_
prefix, so no ze build can carry an upstream opt-out tag, and a build site
that forgot it would link the client in silence. With the constraint inverted,
no ze build sets the tag and none links the client. ErrNoCR still names the
upstream tag in its text; Ze never calls Checkpoint or Restore.

No upstream pull request is opened for this change: upstream's default is the
client built in. The design is docs/architecture/container/runtime.md.

Delete this series when Ze no longer vendors the runtime.

